      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T00:52:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. Using a promisor remote doesn’t require requesting a filter.\n\nThese are separate mechanisms:\n* Filtering asks the server to omit objects matching a filter.\n* Promisor-remote acceptance lets the server omit objects missing locally but available from an accepted promisor remote; the client can fetch them there later.\n\nSo `allowFilter\u003dfalse` means “no client-requested filtering,” not “the response must contain every object.” The client still needs a configured, usable promisor remote to retrieve missing objects.",
      "parentUuid": "124c735a_48a200d1",
      "revId": "aab529bcb74c8c12bd594f2602770f1bbf7e16ed",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
